+# Bug Assessment: Category deletion removes products
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T21:35:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: critical
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+A merchant deleting a category causes products that were only in that category to disappear, breaks carts and orders containing those products, and makes the deleted category return a server error. Deletion must remove only the category subtree and its product-category links; products, inventory, prices, carts, and orders must remain usable. Missing categories must return HTTP 404.
+
+## Symptom
+
+`DELETE /api/v1/private/category/{id}` currently deletes products while deleting a category, including products with no remaining categories, and category reads may fail after deletion instead of returning 404. Expected behavior is to retain products and unlink only the deleted categories, including descendants.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create a category and a product assigned to it; optionally assign the product to another category and place it in a cart or order.
+2. Delete the category through `DELETE /api/v1/private/category/{id}`.
+3. Observe that a product assigned only to the deleted category is deleted, while category lookup by id can produce a server error rather than 404. [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: exact fixture/authentication setup for the reported cart and order flows]
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java:231-284` — category deletion finds products in the category subtree and calls `productService.delete` when the product has no other categories.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/category/CategoryFacadeImpl.java:360-369` — delete-by-id lookup and missing-category handling for the private API.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/category/CategoryFacadeImpl.java:371-385` — category-product listing already rejects a missing category, but depends on the deleted category being removed cleanly.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/category/CategoryApi.java:222-235` — private category deletion endpoint.
+- `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/catalog/product/Product.java:106-134` — product-category many-to-many association that should be updated without deleting the product.
+- `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/catalog/category/Category.java:65-66` — category subtree uses remove cascade, so descendants are deleted with the root.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+The deletion service treats products with no categories outside the target subtree as disposable and explicitly calls `productService.delete`, which removes stock, pricing and other product data referenced by carts and orders. It also performs per-category association updates inconsistently, leaving the category deletion and association cleanup vulnerable to stale persistence state. Confidence: high.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Keep the existing subtree discovery and category deletion cascade, but for every product associated with any category in the subtree remove only those `Category` objects from the product's category set and persist the product. Never call `productService.delete` as a consequence of category deletion, even when no categories remain. Then delete the category root so the descendant categories and their descriptions are removed by the existing cascade. Preserve the facade's 404 behavior for missing category ids and ensure the association cleanup is flushed before the category rows are removed.
+
+Add a regression integration/service test covering a product only in the deleted subtree, a product in both the deleted subtree and a retained category, a descendant category, and missing-category reads/deletes. Assert product retrieval and product data remain available, deleted category ids are absent from product categories, and cart/order entities are unaffected.
+
+**Alternatives** (optional):
+- Remove product-category join rows with a repository bulk operation before deleting categories; this can be more efficient but needs careful transaction ordering and can leave managed entity collections stale.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/category/CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest.java` or a focused service test
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+- Verify deleting a parent removes parent/descendant category associations but retains products with their stock and other categories.
+- Verify products with no remaining categories are still retrievable and carts/orders containing them remain usable.
+- Verify deleted and nonexistent category GET/DELETE requests return 404 and deleted-category product listing is empty.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Deleting categories while products still reference managed category objects can cause foreign-key or stale-session problems; association cleanup must happen in the same transaction before category removal.
+- Products left with no categories may no longer appear in category-based storefront listings, which is expected, but must remain directly retrievable and usable by carts/orders.
+- Existing category subtree cascade behavior must be preserved and scoped to the merchant's category tree.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: exact fixture/authentication setup for the reported cart and order flows]
