+# Bug Fix: Category deletion removes products
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T21:38:00+00:00
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Category deletion now removes only product-category associations for the deleted subtree and retains every product, including products with no remaining categories. Category reads and deletes are store-scoped, and numeric category routes are disambiguated so missing IDs return 404 instead of a server error.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java` | modified | Added a transaction, deduplicated the subtree root, removed target category links only, and removed product deletion. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/category/CategoryFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Uses store-scoped category lookup for ID reads and deletes. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/category/CategoryApi.java` | modified | Constrains numeric ID and friendly URL mappings to prevent ambiguous numeric requests. |
+| `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/category/CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest.java` | added test | Covers retained product, empty category associations, post-delete 404, and repeat-delete 404. |
+
+## Diff Highlights (optional)
+
+Product deletion was replaced with `removeIf` over category IDs followed by `productService.update(dbProduct)`, so stock, price, variants, and other product data are preserved.
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- `CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest.deleteCategoryKeepsProductAndReturnsNotFoundAfterwards` — verifies category deletion does not delete a product and missing category operations return 404.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -DskipTests compile` → passed.
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-shop -Dtest=CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest#deleteCategoryKeepsProductAndReturnsNotFoundAfterwards test` → failed to resolve reactor dependencies from remote Maven repositories (401).
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-shop -am -Dtest=CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest#deleteCategoryKeepsProductAndReturnsNotFoundAfterwards -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → initially failed on the route ambiguity, then passed after route constraints were added.
+- Manual checks: none.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The assessment identified the product-deletion defect and expected 404 behavior but did not identify the ambiguous ID/friendly URL mappings. The focused test exposed that additional routing defect, so both mappings were constrained in `CategoryApi` to make numeric category IDs reliably reach the ID handler.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Extend regression coverage to descendant categories, products shared with retained categories, and cart/order checkout flows.
